node_modules/
dist/
docs/.vitepress/dist/
docs/.vitepress/cache/

# The retrieval index is COMMITTED, deliberately, and this is the note that
# stops someone re-adding it here.
#
# It is a build artifact everywhere else, and this repository is the exception
# because it is also the deployed site. Building it during the deploy would spend
# an embedding request per 32 chunks on every push — against a daily ceiling the
# readers of this site share — so it is built locally and committed instead.
# `test/docs-links.test.js` re-derives the index hash from the docs offline and
# fails when the two disagree, which is what keeps a committed index honest.
#
# A CONSUMER's project should still ignore theirs: `docs/public/rag/` there is a
# pure build artifact with no such tradeoff. `docpilot init` writes that entry.
#
# `rag-local/` is the SAME corpus embedded by a local bge-m3 at 1024 dimensions,
# and it is committed too. It exists to be measured against: an eval run on the
# weaker embedder is a floor, and a configuration that answers well there answers
# at least as well on the stronger one. That comparison is only worth anything if
# both indexes are the same corpus and both are reproducible, which is what
# committing them buys — `test/docs-links.test.js` holds every manifest under
# `docs/public/` to the corpus hash, so neither can drift.
#
# It was ignored because committing it looked like a way to ship keyword-only
# retrieval by accident: the browser asks for the model the manifest names, and
# OpenRouter does not serve `bge-m3`. That is a real failure and it is NOT
# prevented by hiding the file — it is prevented by `readiness()`, which raises
# "the index was built with X, which is not in <provider>'s free embedding pool"
# as a hard `missing`, and by `scripts/vercel-build.sh`, which runs `doctor` and
# turns it into a red build. Serving this index needs an embedder that serves
# bge-m3; nothing else will get past that gate.

.env
.env.local
*.log

# Repo-internal scan output, and one design note kept in Russian for its author.
CLAUDE-SECURITY-RESULTS.md
ui-specs/IDEAS.ru.md

# The Vercel CLI's local link state.
.vercel/

# Both of these are currently excluded only by the author's ~/.gitignore_global,
# so the second person to clone this repository would commit them.
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json

# The embedding cache: float32 vectors `npx docpilot index` has already bought,
# keyed by model and chunk text. Re-derivable at one embedding request per 32
# changed chunks, and larger than the index it saves rebuilding — 1.9 MB per
# embedder here against a 952 KB int8 blob. `docpilot init` writes this line
# into docpilot/.gitignore for a consuming project; this repository has none,
# because it deliberately commits calibration.raw.jsonl.
docpilot/embed-cache/

# The previous eval report, kept aside so a rerun does not erase it. `reportName`
# is a pure function of the inputs, so a rerun with nothing changed writes over
# the very file `previousReport` diffs against. Long-term history is git; this
# directory protects the last run inside ONE working cycle, between the run and
# the decision about what to commit. Same reason as the line above: re-derivable
# by rerunning, and it grows by a report per run.
docpilot/reports/history/
